        "severity": "WARNING",
        "location": "longterm-mem/internal/register/jsonnested.go:48-52",
        "claim": "An existing 1.x user MCP server named \"servers\" is itself an object (mcp.servers = {type:local,...}). The nested container logic treats it as the v2 servers container and splices longterm-mem into that server's definition. nestedValueStart only checks that the value is an object, so no conflict is detected and the user's server entry is corrupted. This was valid input before the change.",
